# Build output
/target

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored. Committing it for a library does not
# affect how downstream crates resolve their dependencies, and it makes CI runs
# reproducible.

# Fuzzing, once there is a target to fuzz. The corpus and the crashes it finds
# are generated data, not sources.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/

# Coverage and profiling output
*.profraw
*.profdata
/lcov.info
/coverage/
/tarpaulin-report.*
/perf.data*
/flamegraph.svg

# Tool leftovers
*.rs.bk
*.orig
*.rej

# Editors
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw?
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# Operating system clutter
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
